          },
          "description": "The BrainBots are out of the classroom and heading back in time to learn as much as they can about dinosaurs. In this card Nellie, Buzz and Gibbs see Diplodocus up close, see a baby one hatch and find out just how many bones make up their long neck, body and tail…. All whilst trying to remind Gibbs that a dinosaur neck is NOT a slide! \n\nTest your knowledge at the end of the card to see how many BrainBank facts you can remember about these amazing creatures. "
